{"type":"message","id":"bf602fc2","parentId":"69b19c93","timestamp":"2026-03-25T10:09:15.108Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"我先拉一下 xixi / aoao 的回包，再给你一版不注水的进度。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0d8886978b870ccc0169c3b447562481918ba764feff3d2dc7\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_AAVa8D6s71Uc2soLzbSA8AC7|fc_0d8886978b870ccc0169c3b44ae2f48191888a18e03ddb69ce","name":"sessions_history","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:xixi:feishu:xixi:direct:ou_7e95c6c474ffd4086e3a05454dd29c24","limit":8,"includeTools":false},"partialJson":"{\"sessionKey\":\"agent:xixi:feishu:xixi:direct:ou_7e95c6c474ffd4086e3a05454dd29c24\",\"limit\":8,\"includeTools\":false}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_avlQCjWDKNzxFJFBHSjMwUhF|fc_0d8886978b870ccc0169c3b44ae3048191bdb5820d2f045621","name":"sessions_history","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506","limit":8,"includeTools":false},"partialJson":"{\"sessionKey\":\"agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506\",\"limit\":8,\"includeTools\":false}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_YtnnMlZClGGib7OekEdpv53Z|fc_0d8886978b870ccc0169c3b44ae3088191a20943f6a09a5c9e","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/project/openclaw-contrib-2026-03-25.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/project/openclaw-contrib-2026-03-25.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":156,"output":200,"cacheRead":24704,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25060,"cost":{"input":0.00039000000000000005,"output":0.003,"cacheRead":0.006176,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.009566}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774433347577}}
{"type":"message","id":"912807fa","parentId":"bf602fc2","timestamp":"2026-03-25T10:09:15.160Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_AAVa8D6s71Uc2soLzbSA8AC7|fc_0d8886978b870ccc0169c3b44ae2f48191888a18e03ddb69ce","toolName":"sessions_history","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"sessionKey\": \"agent:xixi:feishu:xixi:direct:ou_7e95c6c474ffd4086e3a05454dd29c24\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_GwqfHolHqn1jc34Vb1HCZkrn|fc_0cc067ee97d726120169c3657f214c8191acb67223fdf04cd9\",\n          \"name\": \"sessions_send\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"sessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n            \"timeoutSeconds\": 20,\n            \"message\": \"状态：成功\\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，优先补 P1 diagnostics gap issue，并给出 P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\n结果：\\n\\n## 一、P1 issue 需要的证据链（可直接带进 issue）\\n\\n### 1）现象\\n在本地多 Agent + Feishu 群场景里，用户从操作面看到的是：\\n- 群消息进入了某个 agent；\\n- 但当时没有一个“对操作者显而易见的 explicit peer binding”能立刻解释为什么命中的是这个 agent。\\n\\n同时，本地命令面又能看到：\\n- `openclaw agents bindings --json` 中，路由规则可能既有 `peer` 级绑定，也有更宽的 `accountId` 级绑定；\\n- `gateway probe --json` 暴露了 `defaultAgentId: \\\"main\\\"`；\\n- 实际会话中也能看到具体群 session key，例如 `agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3`。\\n\\n这说明：\\n**消息进入某 agent 本身未必异常，但当前缺少一个直接的诊断面来告诉操作者“这次到底是哪个 routing rule 赢了”。**\\n\\n### 2）当前文档缺口\\n当前 docs 已经分别讲了：\\n- routing precedence / bindings / default agent fallback\\n- canonical session key 语义\\n\\n但缺口在于：\\n- 文档没有把“本次实际命中的是 peer binding / account binding / channel fallback / default agent fallback”这件事，以可排障视角讲清；\\n- 文档也没有清楚说明：**最终看到的 session key 只是 routing 结果的归一化载体，不等于能反推这次是哪个 routing rule 命中的。**\\n\\n所以用户容易把：\\n- “看到了某个 agent 的 group session key”\\n误读成：\\n- “一定是路由错了 / 一定是显式绑定命中的 / 一定不是 fallback”。\\n\\n### 3）为什么用户/开发者会误判\\n- 对用户来说：没有显式 group peer binding，直觉上会认为“不该进任何 agent”。\\n- 对开发者来说：看到群消息落到了某个 agent，很容易先怀疑“错误路由”，而不是先怀疑 account/channel/default fallback。\\n- 对排障来说：现有状态面更偏“最后落到哪”，不够偏“为什么落到这”。\\n\\n因此这类现象很容易被误报成 routing bug，但当前证据更稳的结论是：\\n**observability / diagnostics gap**。\\n\\n### 4）最小可复现描述\\n1. 准备一个多 Agent 环境，并确保存在 Feishu 群聊流量。\\n2. 确认配置中没有一个对操作者一眼可见的 group peer binding 能解释该群当前命中的 agent。\\n3. 发送一条群消息，使其进入某 agent。\\n4. 用以下信息交叉核对：\\n   - `openclaw agents bindings --json`\\n   - `openclaw gateway probe --json`\\n   - 实际命中的 session key / agentId\\n5. 观察到：\\n   - 最终能看到“它进了哪个 agent”；\\n   - 但没有直接输出说明“它是通过 peer/account/channel/default 哪一级规则命中的”。\\n\\n注：该现象 **observed in local setup**，并且 **may depend on channel/plugin config, account defaults, and historical bindings**。\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 二、英文 issue 正文 v2（更稳，不预设实现方案）\\n\\n### Title\\nRouting diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent\\n\\n### Body\\n## Summary\\nIn a multi-agent setup, it can be difficult to explain why a specific inbound message ended up in a specific agent.\\n\\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached an agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\\n\\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected. Routing can be influenced by binding specificity, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallbacks, plugin/account defaults, or fallback to the default agent.\\n\\nThe problem here is not yet “routing is wrong”. The problem is that the winning routing path is not easy to inspect.\\n\\n## Why this is confusing\\nFrom an operator’s point of view, these states are easy to confuse:\\n- an explicit peer/group binding matched,\\n- an account-scoped binding matched,\\n- a channel-wide binding or fallback matched,\\n- routing fell back to the default agent,\\n- a historical or less obvious binding still influenced routing.\\n\\nWithout a clear diagnostic surface, expected routing behavior can easily look like a routing bug.\\n\\n## What is currently visible\\nIn local testing, the following pieces can be inspected separately:\\n- routing bindings (`openclaw agents bindings --json`)\\n- default agent information (`openclaw gateway probe --json`)\\n- the final session key / agent that received the message\\n\\nHowever, these surfaces do not make it easy to answer one direct question for a specific inbound message:\\n\\n**Which routing rule actually won?**\\n\\n## Why this matters\\nThis affects:\\n- multi-agent setups\\n- shared group chats\\n- channels that use account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution\\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes\\n\\nIt also makes it harder to distinguish:\\n- a real routing bug\\nfrom\\n- expected fallback behavior that is simply not well explained.\\n\\n## Minimal reproduction description\\nObserved in local setup:\\n1. use a multi-agent environment with Feishu group traffic,\\n2. inspect bindings and config from the operator side,\\n3. send or observe a group message that resolves to a specific agent,\\n4. inspect bindings, default-agent info, and the final session key,\\n5. notice that the final target is visible, but the winning routing path is not directly explained.\\n\\nThis may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings.\\n\\n## Request\\nCould you clarify whether there is already a supported way to inspect the winning inbound routing rule for a given message?\\n\\nIf not, it may be worth improving either:\\n- diagnostics / observability,\\n- docs around routing interpretation,\\nor both.\\n\\nI am intentionally not assuming a specific implementation here. The main ask is to make inbound routing outcomes easier to explain and verify.\\n\\n## Environment\\n- observed in local multi-agent setup\\n- channel: Feishu group\\n- default agent observed in local probe output: `main`\\n- may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 三、P2 docs PR 的最小改动大纲\\n\\n### 目标\\n把“group routing decision”和“canonical session key”明确拆开，减少误判。\\n\\n### 最小改动建议\\n1. **在 `channels/channel-routing` 或对应 session/routing 文档里补一小段解释**\\n   - 先决定 target agent（按 routing precedence）\\n   - 再基于该 agent 生成 canonical group session key\\n   - session key 本身不说明是哪条 routing rule 命中的\\n\\n2. **补一个极短 example block**\\n   - 例子：\\n     - 没有显式 group peer binding\\n     - 但仍可能因为 account/channel/default fallback 路由到某 agent\\n     - 最后 session key 形如 `agent:<agentId>:feishu:group:<id>`\\n\\n3. **在 Feishu / multi-agent 相关文档里补一句边界说明**\\n   - “No explicit peer binding visible” does not necessarily mean “no valid routing path exists”\\n   - routing may still be explained by broader fallback semantics\\n\\n### 建议文件位置\\n- `docs/zh-CN/channels/channel-routing.md`\\n- `docs/zh-CN/channels/feishu.md`\\n- 如英文源也在维护，可同步对应英文文件\\n\\n原因：\\n- 这版 P1 issue 重点放在“当前难解释 routing outcome”，而不是“先声称实现有错”，更符合我们现在的证据强度。\\n- P2 docs PR 不需要大改，只要把 routing decision 与 session identity 的关系讲透，就能明显减少误判。\\n\\n建议：\\n1. 明天优先发 P1 issue。\\n2. issue 发出前，最好再补 3 个具体字段：\\n   - bindings snapshot summary\\n   - default agent summary\\n   - observed final session key\\n3. P2 docs PR 可以随后跟进，作为低风险、容易 merge 的并行产出。\"\n          },\n          \"partialJson\": \"{\\\"sessionKey\\\":\\\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\\\",\\\"timeoutSeconds\\\":20,\\\"message\\\":\\\"状态：成功\\\\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，优先补 P1 diagnostics gap issue，并给出 P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\\\n结果：\\\\n\\\\n## 一、P1 issue 需要的证据链（可直接带进 issue）\\\\n\\\\n### 1）现象\\\\n在本地多 Agent + Feishu 群场景里，用户从操作面看到的是：\\\\n- 群消息进入了某个 agent；\\\\n- 但当时没有一个“对操作者显而易见的 explicit peer binding”能立刻解释为什么命中的是这个 agent。\\\\n\\\\n同时，本地命令面又能看到：\\\\n- `openclaw agents bindings --json` 中，路由规则可能既有 `peer` 级绑定，也有更宽的 `accountId` 级绑定；\\\\n- `gateway probe --json` 暴露了 `defaultAgentId: \\\\\\\"main\\\\\\\"`；\\\\n- 实际会话中也能看到具体群 session key，例如 `agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3`。\\\\n\\\\n这说明：\\\\n**消息进入某 agent 本身未必异常，但当前缺少一个直接的诊断面来告诉操作者“这次到底是哪个 routing rule 赢了”。**\\\\n\\\\n### 2）当前文档缺口\\\\n当前 docs 已经分别讲了：\\\\n- routing precedence / bindings / default agent fallback\\\\n- canonical session key 语义\\\\n\\\\n但缺口在于：\\\\n- 文档没有把“本次实际命中的是 peer binding / account binding / channel fallback / default agent fallback”这件事，以可排障视角讲清；\\\\n- 文档也没有清楚说明：**最终看到的 session key 只是 routing 结果的归一化载体，不等于能反推这次是哪个 routing rule 命中的。**\\\\n\\\\n所以用户容易把：\\\\n- “看到了某个 agent 的 group session key”\\\\n误读成：\\\\n- “一定是路由错了 / 一定是显式绑定命中的 / 一定不是 fallback”。\\\\n\\\\n### 3）为什么用户/开发者会误判\\\\n- 对用户来说：没有显式 group peer binding，直觉上会认为“不该进任何 agent”。\\\\n- 对开发者来说：看到群消息落到了某个 agent，很容易先怀疑“错误路由”，而不是先怀疑 account/channel/default fallback。\\\\n- 对排障来说：现有状态面更偏“最后落到哪”，不够偏“为什么落到这”。\\\\n\\\\n因此这类现象很容易被误报成 routing bug，但当前证据更稳的结论是：\\\\n**observability / diagnostics gap**。\\\\n\\\\n### 4）最小可复现描述\\\\n1. 准备一个多 Agent 环境，并确保存在 Feishu 群聊流量。\\\\n2. 确认配置中没有一个对操作者一眼可见的 group peer binding 能解释该群当前命中的 agent。\\\\n3. 发送一条群消息，使其进入某 agent。\\\\n4. 用以下信息交叉核对：\\\\n   - `openclaw agents bindings --json`\\\\n   - `openclaw gateway probe --json`\\\\n   - 实际命中的 session key / agentId\\\\n5. 观察到：\\\\n   - 最终能看到“它进了哪个 agent”；\\\\n   - 但没有直接输出说明“它是通过 peer/account/channel/default 哪一级规则命中的”。\\\\n\\\\n注：该现象 **observed in local setup**，并且 **may depend on channel/plugin config, account defaults, and historical bindings**。\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 二、英文 issue 正文 v2（更稳，不预设实现方案）\\\\n\\\\n### Title\\\\nRouting diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent\\\\n\\\\n### Body\\\\n## Summary\\\\nIn a multi-agent setup, it can be difficult to explain why a specific inbound message ended up in a specific agent.\\\\n\\\\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached an agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\\\\n\\\\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected. Routing can be influenced by binding specificity, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallbacks, plugin/account defaults, or fallback to the default agent.\\\\n\\\\nThe problem here is not yet “routing is wrong”. The problem is that the winning routing path is not easy to inspect.\\\\n\\\\n## Why this is confusing\\\\nFrom an operator’s point of view, these states are easy to confuse:\\\\n- an explicit peer/group binding matched,\\\\n- an account-scoped binding matched,\\\\n- a channel-wide binding or fallback matched,\\\\n- routing fell back to the default agent,\\\\n- a historical or less obvious binding still influenced routing.\\\\n\\\\nWithout a clear diagnostic surface, expected routing behavior can easily look like a routing bug.\\\\n\\\\n## What is currently visible\\\\nIn local testing, the following pieces can be inspected separately:\\\\n- routing bindings (`openclaw agents bindings --json`)\\\\n- default agent information (`openclaw gateway probe --json`)\\\\n- the final session key / agent that received the message\\\\n\\\\nHowever, these surfaces do not make it easy to answer one direct question for a specific inbound message:\\\\n\\\\n**Which routing rule actually won?**\\\\n\\\\n## Why this matters\\\\nThis affects:\\\\n- multi-agent setups\\\\n- shared group chats\\\\n- channels that use account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution\\\\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes\\\\n\\\\nIt also makes it harder to distinguish:\\\\n- a real routing bug\\\\nfrom\\\\n- expected fallback behavior that is simply not well explained.\\\\n\\\\n## Minimal reproduction description\\\\nObserved in local\\n…(truncated)…\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n      \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413179857\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \" 已完成并回 main，但 `sessions_send` 仍超时。\\n\\n本轮我补了 3 块可直接用的内容：\\n\\n1. **P1 issue 证据链**\\n- 现象：群消息进了某 agent，但操作者看不到“哪条 routing rule 赢了”\\n- 文档缺口：docs 分别讲了 routing 和 session key，但没讲清“session key 不等于可反推命中的 rule”\\n- 误判原因：用户会把 fallback / account binding / channel binding 误判成 bug\\n- 最小复现：bindings + default agent + final session key 三者交叉看，能看到结果，看不到“为什么”\\n\\n2. **英文 issue 正文 v2**\\n- 标题已收敛为更稳的：\\n  **Routing diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\\n- 重点放在 observability gap，不预设实现方案\\n\\n3. **P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲**\\n- 拆清 `routing decision` 和 `canonical session key`\\n- 补一个极短 example block\\n- 在 `channel-routing` / `feishu` 文档补一句：\\n  “No explicit peer binding visible” 不等于 “no valid routing path exists”\\n\\n如果你要，我下一条可以直接把这份 issue v2 压缩成 GitHub 可直接粘贴的最终版。\",\n          \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_0cc067ee97d726120169c365ba3b508191a9e1f4e312e0a1ce\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"final_answer\\\"}\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n      \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413239502\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"继续执行，不用等我。\\n任务优先级：P1 > P2。\\n请直接产出可贴 GitHub 的英文内容。\\n\\n交付 A：P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\\n要求：\\n- 标题 3 个备选\\n- 正文按 Background / What is unclear / Why this matters / Suggested improvement 四段\\n- 明确避免把它写成 confirmed bug\\n- 给 1 段 minimal reproduction（抽象描述即可）\\n\\n交付 B：P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\n要求：\\n- 要改哪些文档位置\\n- 每处补什么一句话\\n- 为什么这是最小可合并版本\\n\\n按“状态/任务/结果/原因/建议”直接回 main。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413579221,\n      \"provenance\": {\n        \"kind\": \"inter_session\",\n        \"sourceSessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3\",\n        \"sourceChannel\": \"feishu\",\n        \"sourceTool\": \"sessions_send\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"我直接按 GitHub 可贴格式整理 P1 issue v2 和 P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲，并回 main。\",\n          \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_0cc067ee97d726120169c3670e90288191926b73d3846f5017\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_DnGSEILD85JAnLauJihSSK48|fc_0cc067ee97d726120169c3670e9d008191aae9acd6dcf34952\",\n          \"name\": \"sessions_send\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"sessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n            \"timeoutSeconds\": 20,\n            \"message\": \"状态：成功\\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，直接产出可贴 GitHub 的英文内容（P1 > P2）\\n结果：\\n\\n## 交付 A：P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\\n\\n### Title options\\n1. **Routing diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\\n2. **Observability gap: inbound routing outcomes are hard to explain in multi-agent setups**\\n3. **Docs/diagnostics gap: inbound routing may be correct, but the winning routing path is hard to inspect**\\n\\n### Body\\n#### Background\\nIn a multi-agent setup, an inbound message can reach a specific agent through several valid routing paths, including peer-specific bindings, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallback, or fallback to the default agent.\\n\\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached a specific agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\\n\\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected behavior. The issue here is not that routing is confirmed to be wrong. The issue is that it is hard to explain which routing path actually won for a specific inbound message.\\n\\n#### What is unclear\\nFrom the operator side, it is difficult to tell whether a given inbound message:\\n- matched an explicit peer/group binding,\\n- matched an account-scoped binding,\\n- matched a channel-wide binding or fallback,\\n- resolved via plugin/account defaults,\\n- or fell back to the default agent.\\n\\nCurrent surfaces can show related information separately, such as:\\n- configured bindings,\\n- default agent information,\\n- the final agent/session that received the message.\\n\\nBut they do not clearly answer one question for a specific inbound message:\\n\\n**Which routing rule actually determined the target agent?**\\n\\n#### Why this matters\\nThis makes it easy to misclassify expected behavior as a routing bug.\\n\\nIt especially affects:\\n- multi-agent setups,\\n- shared group chats,\\n- channels with account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution,\\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes.\\n\\nIt also makes it harder for both users and contributors to distinguish between:\\n- a real routing defect,\\n- expected fallback behavior,\\n- and a docs/diagnostics gap.\\n\\n#### Suggested improvement\\nI am intentionally not treating this as a confirmed bug or assuming a specific implementation.\\n\\nThe request is narrower: make inbound routing outcomes easier to explain and verify.\\n\\nThat could mean improving one or more of the following:\\n- diagnostics,\\n- observability,\\n- logs/status output,\\n- or docs that explain how to interpret routing outcomes.\\n\\nThe main goal is to make it easier to answer, for a specific inbound message:\\n- which routing path won,\\n- whether fallback was involved,\\n- and whether the observed outcome is expected.\\n\\n#### Minimal reproduction\\nObserved in local setup:\\n1. use a multi-agent environment with group traffic,\\n2. inspect visible bindings/config from the operator side,\\n3. send or observe an inbound group message that resolves to a specific agent,\\n4. inspect the final target agent/session,\\n5. notice that the final outcome is visible, but the winning routing path is not directly explained.\\n\\nThis may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 交付 B：P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\n\\n### 1) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md`（或对应 zh-CN 同位置）\\n**补一句：**\\n> The canonical session key shows the final routed target, but it does not by itself explain which routing rule matched.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n先把“session key 不是 routing rule 解释器”讲清。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md` 中 session key / routing precedence 相邻位置\\n**补一句：**\\n> For group chats, OpenClaw first resolves the target agent using routing precedence, then derives the canonical group session key from that result.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n明确先后顺序：先路由，后生成 canonical session key。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3) `docs/channels/feishu.md` 的 multi-agent routing / group routing 相关段落\\n**补一句：**\\n> If no explicit group peer binding is visible, routing may still be explained by broader account/channel fallback semantics, depending on configuration.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n把 Feishu 用户最容易误判的点补上，但不把话说死，不越过证据边界。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4) 可选：在 multi-agent / session docs 中补一个极短 example block\\n**补一句示例：**\\n> Example: a group message may end up in `agent:<agentId>:feishu:group:<id>` even when there is no peer-specific group binding, if routing resolved through a broader fallback path.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n给一个最短例子，降低理解门槛。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 为什么这是最小可合并版本\\n- 不改 routing 逻辑，只补解释层。\\n- 不要求新增命令或诊断面，review 风险低。\\n- 每处只补 1 句话，维护成本低。\\n- 能直接减少两个高频误判：\\n  1. “没有显式 group binding = 不该路由到任何 agent”\\n  2. “看到了 session key = 就能反推出哪条 routing rule 命中”\\n\\n原因：\\n- P1 当前最稳的推进方式，是把问题收敛为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是过早定性成 confirmed bug。\\n- P2 适合先走最小 docs 修正，低风险、容易 merge，也能和 P1 形成一主一辅的推进组合。\\n\\n建议：\\n1. P1 issue 优先用标题 1。\\n2. P2 docs PR 先做最小版，只补解释，不扩大到全面重写 routing 文档。\\n3. 若后续拿到更硬证据，再决定是否把 P1 从 diagnostics gap 升级成更具体的产品问题。\"\n          },\n          \"partialJson\": \"{\\\"sessionKey\\\":\\\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\\\",\\\"timeoutSeconds\\\":20,\\\"message\\\":\\\"状态：成功\\\\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，直接产出可贴 GitHub 的英文内容（P1 > P2）\\\\n结果：\\\\n\\\\n## 交付 A：P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\\\\n\\\\n### Title options\\\\n1. **Routing diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\\\\n2. **Observability gap: inbound routing outcomes are hard to explain in multi-agent setups**\\\\n3. **Docs/diagnostics gap: inbound routing may be correct, but the winning routing path is hard to inspect**\\\\n\\\\n### Body\\\\n#### Background\\\\nIn a multi-agent setup, an inbound message can reach a specific agent through several valid routing paths, including peer-specific bindings, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallback, or fallback to the default agent.\\\\n\\\\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached a specific agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\\\\n\\\\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected behavior. The issue here is not that routing is confirmed to be wrong. The issue is that it is hard to explain which routing path actually won for a specific inbound message.\\\\n\\\\n#### What is unclear\\\\nFrom the operator side, it is difficult to tell whether a given inbound message:\\\\n- matched an explicit peer/group binding,\\\\n- matched an account-scoped binding,\\\\n- matched a channel-wide binding or fallback,\\\\n- resolved via plugin/account defaults,\\\\n- or fell back to the default agent.\\\\n\\\\nCurrent surfaces can show related information separately, such as:\\\\n- configured bindings,\\\\n- default agent information,\\\\n- the final agent/session that received the message.\\\\n\\\\nBut they do not clearly answer one question for a specific inbound message:\\\\n\\\\n**Which routing rule actually determined the target agent?**\\\\n\\\\n#### Why this matters\\\\nThis makes it easy to misclassify expected behavior as a routing bug.\\\\n\\\\nIt especially affects:\\\\n- multi-agent setups,\\\\n- shared group chats,\\\\n- channels with account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution,\\\\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes.\\\\n\\\\nIt also makes it harder for both users and contributors to distinguish between:\\\\n- a real routing defect,\\\\n- expected fallback behavior,\\\\n- and a docs/diagnostics gap.\\\\n\\\\n#### Suggested improvement\\\\nI am intentionally not treating this as a confirmed bug or assuming a specific implementation.\\\\n\\\\nThe request is narrower: make inbound routing outcomes easier to explain and verify.\\\\n\\\\nThat could mean improving one or more of the following:\\\\n- diagnostics,\\\\n- observability,\\\\n- logs/status output,\\\\n- or docs that explain how to interpret routing outcomes.\\\\n\\\\nThe main goal is to make it easier to answer, for a specific inbound message:\\\\n- which routing path won,\\\\n- whether fallback was involved,\\\\n- and whether the observed outcome is expected.\\\\n\\\\n#### Minimal reproduction\\\\nObserved in local setup:\\\\n1. use a multi-agent environment with group traffic,\\\\n2. inspect visible bindings/config from the operator side,\\\\n3. send or observe an inbound group message that resolves to a specific agent,\\\\n4. inspect the final target agent/session,\\\\n5. notice that the final outcome is visible, but the winning routing path is not directly explained.\\\\n\\\\nThis may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 交付 B：P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\\\n\\\\n### 1) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md`（或对应 zh-CN 同位置）\\\\n**补一句：**\\\\n> The canonical session key shows the final routed target, but it does not by itself explain which routing rule matched.\\\\n\\\\n**作用：**\\\\n先把“session key 不是 routing rule 解释器”讲清。\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 2) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md` 中 session key / routing precedence 相邻位置\\\\n**补一句：**\\\\n> For group chats, OpenClaw first resolves the target agent using routing precedence, then derives the canonical group session key from that result.\\\\n\\\\n**作用：**\\\\n明确先后顺序：先路由，后生成 canonical\\n…(truncated)…\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n      \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413579225\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \" 已继续完成并回 main，但 `sessions_send` 仍超时。\\n\\n本次已产出两份可直接贴 GitHub 的内容：\\n\\n### A. P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\\n包含：\\n- **3 个标题备选**\\n- 正文按：\\n  - Background\\n  - What is unclear\\n  - Why this matters\\n  - Suggested improvement\\n- 明确写了：\\n  - **this is not being presented as a confirmed bug**\\n- 另附：\\n  - **1 段 minimal reproduction**\\n\\n### B. P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\n包含：\\n- **要改哪些文档位置**\\n- **每处补什么一句话**\\n- **为什么这是最小可合并版本**\\n\\n如果你要，我下一条可以把 **P1 issue 最终英文版** 单独再压成一份无解释、可直接复制提交的纯净文本。\",\n          \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_0cc067ee97d726120169c3673d9a048191998d2084f475b4c5\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"final_answer\\\"}\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n      \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413627576\n    }\n  ],\n  \"truncated\": true,\n  \"droppedMessages\": false,\n  \"contentTruncated\": true,\n  \"contentRedacted\": true,\n  \"bytes\": 27994\n}"}],"details":{"sessionKey":"agent:xixi:feishu:xixi:direct:ou_7e95c6c474ffd4086e3a05454dd29c24","messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_GwqfHolHqn1jc34Vb1HCZkrn|fc_0cc067ee97d726120169c3657f214c8191acb67223fdf04cd9","name":"sessions_send","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8","timeoutSeconds":20,"message":"状态：成功\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，优先补 P1 diagnostics gap issue，并给出 P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\n结果：\n\n## 一、P1 issue 需要的证据链（可直接带进 issue）\n\n### 1）现象\n在本地多 Agent + Feishu 群场景里，用户从操作面看到的是：\n- 群消息进入了某个 agent；\n- 但当时没有一个“对操作者显而易见的 explicit peer binding”能立刻解释为什么命中的是这个 agent。\n\n同时，本地命令面又能看到：\n- `openclaw agents bindings --json` 中，路由规则可能既有 `peer` 级绑定，也有更宽的 `accountId` 级绑定；\n- `gateway probe --json` 暴露了 `defaultAgentId: \"main\"`；\n- 实际会话中也能看到具体群 session key，例如 `agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3`。\n\n这说明：\n**消息进入某 agent 本身未必异常，但当前缺少一个直接的诊断面来告诉操作者“这次到底是哪个 routing rule 赢了”。**\n\n### 2）当前文档缺口\n当前 docs 已经分别讲了：\n- routing precedence / bindings / default agent fallback\n- canonical session key 语义\n\n但缺口在于：\n- 文档没有把“本次实际命中的是 peer binding / account binding / channel fallback / default agent fallback”这件事，以可排障视角讲清；\n- 文档也没有清楚说明：**最终看到的 session key 只是 routing 结果的归一化载体，不等于能反推这次是哪个 routing rule 命中的。**\n\n所以用户容易把：\n- “看到了某个 agent 的 group session key”\n误读成：\n- “一定是路由错了 / 一定是显式绑定命中的 / 一定不是 fallback”。\n\n### 3）为什么用户/开发者会误判\n- 对用户来说：没有显式 group peer binding，直觉上会认为“不该进任何 agent”。\n- 对开发者来说：看到群消息落到了某个 agent，很容易先怀疑“错误路由”，而不是先怀疑 account/channel/default fallback。\n- 对排障来说：现有状态面更偏“最后落到哪”，不够偏“为什么落到这”。\n\n因此这类现象很容易被误报成 routing bug，但当前证据更稳的结论是：\n**observability / diagnostics gap**。\n\n### 4）最小可复现描述\n1. 准备一个多 Agent 环境，并确保存在 Feishu 群聊流量。\n2. 确认配置中没有一个对操作者一眼可见的 group peer binding 能解释该群当前命中的 agent。\n3. 发送一条群消息，使其进入某 agent。\n4. 用以下信息交叉核对：\n   - `openclaw agents bindings --json`\n   - `openclaw gateway probe --json`\n   - 实际命中的 session key / agentId\n5. 观察到：\n   - 最终能看到“它进了哪个 agent”；\n   - 但没有直接输出说明“它是通过 peer/account/channel/default 哪一级规则命中的”。\n\n注：该现象 **observed in local setup**，并且 **may depend on channel/plugin config, account defaults, and historical bindings**。\n\n---\n\n## 二、英文 issue 正文 v2（更稳，不预设实现方案）\n\n### Title\nRouting diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent\n\n### Body\n## Summary\nIn a multi-agent setup, it can be difficult to explain why a specific inbound message ended up in a specific agent.\n\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached an agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\n\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected. Routing can be influenced by binding specificity, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallbacks, plugin/account defaults, or fallback to the default agent.\n\nThe problem here is not yet “routing is wrong”. The problem is that the winning routing path is not easy to inspect.\n\n## Why this is confusing\nFrom an operator’s point of view, these states are easy to confuse:\n- an explicit peer/group binding matched,\n- an account-scoped binding matched,\n- a channel-wide binding or fallback matched,\n- routing fell back to the default agent,\n- a historical or less obvious binding still influenced routing.\n\nWithout a clear diagnostic surface, expected routing behavior can easily look like a routing bug.\n\n## What is currently visible\nIn local testing, the following pieces can be inspected separately:\n- routing bindings (`openclaw agents bindings --json`)\n- default agent information (`openclaw gateway probe --json`)\n- the final session key / agent that received the message\n\nHowever, these surfaces do not make it easy to answer one direct question for a specific inbound message:\n\n**Which routing rule actually won?**\n\n## Why this matters\nThis affects:\n- multi-agent setups\n- shared group chats\n- channels that use account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes\n\nIt also makes it harder to distinguish:\n- a real routing bug\nfrom\n- expected fallback behavior that is simply not well explained.\n\n## Minimal reproduction description\nObserved in local setup:\n1. use a multi-agent environment with Feishu group traffic,\n2. inspect bindings and config from the operator side,\n3. send or observe a group message that resolves to a specific agent,\n4. inspect bindings, default-agent info, and the final session key,\n5. notice that the final target is visible, but the winning routing path is not directly explained.\n\nThis may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings.\n\n## Request\nCould you clarify whether there is already a supported way to inspect the winning inbound routing rule for a given message?\n\nIf not, it may be worth improving either:\n- diagnostics / observability,\n- docs around routing interpretation,\nor both.\n\nI am intentionally not assuming a specific implementation here. The main ask is to make inbound routing outcomes easier to explain and verify.\n\n## Environment\n- observed in local multi-agent setup\n- channel: Feishu group\n- default agent observed in local probe output: `main`\n- may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings\n\n---\n\n## 三、P2 docs PR 的最小改动大纲\n\n### 目标\n把“group routing decision”和“canonical session key”明确拆开，减少误判。\n\n### 最小改动建议\n1. **在 `channels/channel-routing` 或对应 session/routing 文档里补一小段解释**\n   - 先决定 target agent（按 routing precedence）\n   - 再基于该 agent 生成 canonical group session key\n   - session key 本身不说明是哪条 routing rule 命中的\n\n2. **补一个极短 example block**\n   - 例子：\n     - 没有显式 group peer binding\n     - 但仍可能因为 account/channel/default fallback 路由到某 agent\n     - 最后 session key 形如 `agent:<agentId>:feishu:group:<id>`\n\n3. **在 Feishu / multi-agent 相关文档里补一句边界说明**\n   - “No explicit peer binding visible” does not necessarily mean “no valid routing path exists”\n   - routing may still be explained by broader fallback semantics\n\n### 建议文件位置\n- `docs/zh-CN/channels/channel-routing.md`\n- `docs/zh-CN/channels/feishu.md`\n- 如英文源也在维护，可同步对应英文文件\n\n原因：\n- 这版 P1 issue 重点放在“当前难解释 routing outcome”，而不是“先声称实现有错”，更符合我们现在的证据强度。\n- P2 docs PR 不需要大改，只要把 routing decision 与 session identity 的关系讲透，就能明显减少误判。\n\n建议：\n1. 明天优先发 P1 issue。\n2. issue 发出前，最好再补 3 个具体字段：\n   - bindings snapshot summary\n   - default agent summary\n   - observed final session key\n3. P2 docs PR 可以随后跟进，作为低风险、容易 merge 的并行产出。"},"partialJson":"{\"sessionKey\":\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\"timeoutSeconds\":20,\"message\":\"状态：成功\\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，优先补 P1 diagnostics gap issue，并给出 P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\n结果：\\n\\n## 一、P1 issue 需要的证据链（可直接带进 issue）\\n\\n### 1）现象\\n在本地多 Agent + Feishu 群场景里，用户从操作面看到的是：\\n- 群消息进入了某个 agent；\\n- 但当时没有一个“对操作者显而易见的 explicit peer binding”能立刻解释为什么命中的是这个 agent。\\n\\n同时，本地命令面又能看到：\\n- `openclaw agents bindings --json` 中，路由规则可能既有 `peer` 级绑定，也有更宽的 `accountId` 级绑定；\\n- `gateway probe --json` 暴露了 `defaultAgentId: \\\"main\\\"`；\\n- 实际会话中也能看到具体群 session key，例如 `agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3`。\\n\\n这说明：\\n**消息进入某 agent 本身未必异常，但当前缺少一个直接的诊断面来告诉操作者“这次到底是哪个 routing rule 赢了”。**\\n\\n### 2）当前文档缺口\\n当前 docs 已经分别讲了：\\n- routing precedence / bindings / default agent fallback\\n- canonical session key 语义\\n\\n但缺口在于：\\n- 文档没有把“本次实际命中的是 peer binding / account binding / channel fallback / default agent fallback”这件事，以可排障视角讲清；\\n- 文档也没有清楚说明：**最终看到的 session key 只是 routing 结果的归一化载体，不等于能反推这次是哪个 routing rule 命中的。**\\n\\n所以用户容易把：\\n- “看到了某个 agent 的 group session key”\\n误读成：\\n- “一定是路由错了 / 一定是显式绑定命中的 / 一定不是 fallback”。\\n\\n### 3）为什么用户/开发者会误判\\n- 对用户来说：没有显式 group peer binding，直觉上会认为“不该进任何 agent”。\\n- 对开发者来说：看到群消息落到了某个 agent，很容易先怀疑“错误路由”，而不是先怀疑 account/channel/default fallback。\\n- 对排障来说：现有状态面更偏“最后落到哪”，不够偏“为什么落到这”。\\n\\n因此这类现象很容易被误报成 routing bug，但当前证据更稳的结论是：\\n**observability / diagnostics gap**。\\n\\n### 4）最小可复现描述\\n1. 准备一个多 Agent 环境，并确保存在 Feishu 群聊流量。\\n2. 确认配置中没有一个对操作者一眼可见的 group peer binding 能解释该群当前命中的 agent。\\n3. 发送一条群消息，使其进入某 agent。\\n4. 用以下信息交叉核对：\\n   - `openclaw agents bindings --json`\\n   - `openclaw gateway probe --json`\\n   - 实际命中的 session key / agentId\\n5. 观察到：\\n   - 最终能看到“它进了哪个 agent”；\\n   - 但没有直接输出说明“它是通过 peer/account/channel/default 哪一级规则命中的”。\\n\\n注：该现象 **observed in local setup**，并且 **may depend on channel/plugin config, account defaults, and historical bindings**。\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 二、英文 issue 正文 v2（更稳，不预设实现方案）\\n\\n### Title\\nRouting diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent\\n\\n### Body\\n## Summary\\nIn a multi-agent setup, it can be difficult to explain why a specific inbound message ended up in a specific agent.\\n\\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached an agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\\n\\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected. Routing can be influenced by binding specificity, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallbacks, plugin/account defaults, or fallback to the default agent.\\n\\nThe problem here is not yet “routing is wrong”. The problem is that the winning routing path is not easy to inspect.\\n\\n## Why this is confusing\\nFrom an operator’s point of view, these states are easy to confuse:\\n- an explicit peer/group binding matched,\\n- an account-scoped binding matched,\\n- a channel-wide binding or fallback matched,\\n- routing fell back to the default agent,\\n- a historical or less obvious binding still influenced routing.\\n\\nWithout a clear diagnostic surface, expected routing behavior can easily look like a routing bug.\\n\\n## What is currently visible\\nIn local testing, the following pieces can be inspected separately:\\n- routing bindings (`openclaw agents bindings --json`)\\n- default agent information (`openclaw gateway probe --json`)\\n- the final session key / agent that received the message\\n\\nHowever, these surfaces do not make it easy to answer one direct question for a specific inbound message:\\n\\n**Which routing rule actually won?**\\n\\n## Why this matters\\nThis affects:\\n- multi-agent setups\\n- shared group chats\\n- channels that use account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution\\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes\\n\\nIt also makes it harder to distinguish:\\n- a real routing bug\\nfrom\\n- expected fallback behavior that is simply not well explained.\\n\\n## Minimal reproduction description\\nObserved in local\n…(truncated)…"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774413179857},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" 已完成并回 main，但 `sessions_send` 仍超时。\n\n本轮我补了 3 块可直接用的内容：\n\n1. **P1 issue 证据链**\n- 现象：群消息进了某 agent，但操作者看不到“哪条 routing rule 赢了”\n- 文档缺口：docs 分别讲了 routing 和 session key，但没讲清“session key 不等于可反推命中的 rule”\n- 误判原因：用户会把 fallback / account binding / channel binding 误判成 bug\n- 最小复现：bindings + default agent + final session key 三者交叉看，能看到结果，看不到“为什么”\n\n2. **英文 issue 正文 v2**\n- 标题已收敛为更稳的：\n  **Routing diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\n- 重点放在 observability gap，不预设实现方案\n\n3. **P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲**\n- 拆清 `routing decision` 和 `canonical session key`\n- 补一个极短 example block\n- 在 `channel-routing` / `feishu` 文档补一句：\n  “No explicit peer binding visible” 不等于 “no valid routing path exists”\n\n如果你要，我下一条可以直接把这份 issue v2 压缩成 GitHub 可直接粘贴的最终版。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0cc067ee97d726120169c365ba3b508191a9e1f4e312e0a1ce\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774413239502},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"继续执行，不用等我。\n任务优先级：P1 > P2。\n请直接产出可贴 GitHub 的英文内容。\n\n交付 A：P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\n要求：\n- 标题 3 个备选\n- 正文按 Background / What is unclear / Why this matters / Suggested improvement 四段\n- 明确避免把它写成 confirmed bug\n- 给 1 段 minimal reproduction（抽象描述即可）\n\n交付 B：P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\n要求：\n- 要改哪些文档位置\n- 每处补什么一句话\n- 为什么这是最小可合并版本\n\n按“状态/任务/结果/原因/建议”直接回 main。"}],"timestamp":1774413579221,"provenance":{"kind":"inter_session","sourceSessionKey":"agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3","sourceChannel":"feishu","sourceTool":"sessions_send"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":""},{"type":"text","text":"我直接按 GitHub 可贴格式整理 P1 issue v2 和 P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲，并回 main。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0cc067ee97d726120169c3670e90288191926b73d3846f5017\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_DnGSEILD85JAnLauJihSSK48|fc_0cc067ee97d726120169c3670e9d008191aae9acd6dcf34952","name":"sessions_send","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8","timeoutSeconds":20,"message":"状态：成功\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，直接产出可贴 GitHub 的英文内容（P1 > P2）\n结果：\n\n## 交付 A：P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\n\n### Title options\n1. **Routing diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\n2. **Observability gap: inbound routing outcomes are hard to explain in multi-agent setups**\n3. **Docs/diagnostics gap: inbound routing may be correct, but the winning routing path is hard to inspect**\n\n### Body\n#### Background\nIn a multi-agent setup, an inbound message can reach a specific agent through several valid routing paths, including peer-specific bindings, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallback, or fallback to the default agent.\n\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached a specific agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\n\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected behavior. The issue here is not that routing is confirmed to be wrong. The issue is that it is hard to explain which routing path actually won for a specific inbound message.\n\n#### What is unclear\nFrom the operator side, it is difficult to tell whether a given inbound message:\n- matched an explicit peer/group binding,\n- matched an account-scoped binding,\n- matched a channel-wide binding or fallback,\n- resolved via plugin/account defaults,\n- or fell back to the default agent.\n\nCurrent surfaces can show related information separately, such as:\n- configured bindings,\n- default agent information,\n- the final agent/session that received the message.\n\nBut they do not clearly answer one question for a specific inbound message:\n\n**Which routing rule actually determined the target agent?**\n\n#### Why this matters\nThis makes it easy to misclassify expected behavior as a routing bug.\n\nIt especially affects:\n- multi-agent setups,\n- shared group chats,\n- channels with account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution,\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes.\n\nIt also makes it harder for both users and contributors to distinguish between:\n- a real routing defect,\n- expected fallback behavior,\n- and a docs/diagnostics gap.\n\n#### Suggested improvement\nI am intentionally not treating this as a confirmed bug or assuming a specific implementation.\n\nThe request is narrower: make inbound routing outcomes easier to explain and verify.\n\nThat could mean improving one or more of the following:\n- diagnostics,\n- observability,\n- logs/status output,\n- or docs that explain how to interpret routing outcomes.\n\nThe main goal is to make it easier to answer, for a specific inbound message:\n- which routing path won,\n- whether fallback was involved,\n- and whether the observed outcome is expected.\n\n#### Minimal reproduction\nObserved in local setup:\n1. use a multi-agent environment with group traffic,\n2. inspect visible bindings/config from the operator side,\n3. send or observe an inbound group message that resolves to a specific agent,\n4. inspect the final target agent/session,\n5. notice that the final outcome is visible, but the winning routing path is not directly explained.\n\nThis may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings.\n\n---\n\n## 交付 B：P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\n\n### 1) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md`（或对应 zh-CN 同位置）\n**补一句：**\n> The canonical session key shows the final routed target, but it does not by itself explain which routing rule matched.\n\n**作用：**\n先把“session key 不是 routing rule 解释器”讲清。\n\n---\n\n### 2) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md` 中 session key / routing precedence 相邻位置\n**补一句：**\n> For group chats, OpenClaw first resolves the target agent using routing precedence, then derives the canonical group session key from that result.\n\n**作用：**\n明确先后顺序：先路由，后生成 canonical session key。\n\n---\n\n### 3) `docs/channels/feishu.md` 的 multi-agent routing / group routing 相关段落\n**补一句：**\n> If no explicit group peer binding is visible, routing may still be explained by broader account/channel fallback semantics, depending on configuration.\n\n**作用：**\n把 Feishu 用户最容易误判的点补上，但不把话说死，不越过证据边界。\n\n---\n\n### 4) 可选：在 multi-agent / session docs 中补一个极短 example block\n**补一句示例：**\n> Example: a group message may end up in `agent:<agentId>:feishu:group:<id>` even when there is no peer-specific group binding, if routing resolved through a broader fallback path.\n\n**作用：**\n给一个最短例子，降低理解门槛。\n\n---\n\n### 为什么这是最小可合并版本\n- 不改 routing 逻辑，只补解释层。\n- 不要求新增命令或诊断面，review 风险低。\n- 每处只补 1 句话，维护成本低。\n- 能直接减少两个高频误判：\n  1. “没有显式 group binding = 不该路由到任何 agent”\n  2. “看到了 session key = 就能反推出哪条 routing rule 命中”\n\n原因：\n- P1 当前最稳的推进方式，是把问题收敛为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是过早定性成 confirmed bug。\n- P2 适合先走最小 docs 修正，低风险、容易 merge，也能和 P1 形成一主一辅的推进组合。\n\n建议：\n1. P1 issue 优先用标题 1。\n2. P2 docs PR 先做最小版，只补解释，不扩大到全面重写 routing 文档。\n3. 若后续拿到更硬证据，再决定是否把 P1 从 diagnostics gap 升级成更具体的产品问题。"},"partialJson":"{\"sessionKey\":\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\"timeoutSeconds\":20,\"message\":\"状态：成功\\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，直接产出可贴 GitHub 的英文内容（P1 > P2）\\n结果：\\n\\n## 交付 A：P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\\n\\n### Title options\\n1. **Routing diagnostics gap: it is hard to tell whether inbound traffic matched a binding or fell back to the default agent**\\n2. **Observability gap: inbound routing outcomes are hard to explain in multi-agent setups**\\n3. **Docs/diagnostics gap: inbound routing may be correct, but the winning routing path is hard to inspect**\\n\\n### Body\\n#### Background\\nIn a multi-agent setup, an inbound message can reach a specific agent through several valid routing paths, including peer-specific bindings, account-scoped bindings, channel-wide fallback, or fallback to the default agent.\\n\\nObserved in local setup: inbound Feishu group traffic reached a specific agent even when there was no immediately obvious explicit peer-level binding visible from the operator’s point of view.\\n\\nBased on the current docs, this may still be expected behavior. The issue here is not that routing is confirmed to be wrong. The issue is that it is hard to explain which routing path actually won for a specific inbound message.\\n\\n#### What is unclear\\nFrom the operator side, it is difficult to tell whether a given inbound message:\\n- matched an explicit peer/group binding,\\n- matched an account-scoped binding,\\n- matched a channel-wide binding or fallback,\\n- resolved via plugin/account defaults,\\n- or fell back to the default agent.\\n\\nCurrent surfaces can show related information separately, such as:\\n- configured bindings,\\n- default agent information,\\n- the final agent/session that received the message.\\n\\nBut they do not clearly answer one question for a specific inbound message:\\n\\n**Which routing rule actually determined the target agent?**\\n\\n#### Why this matters\\nThis makes it easy to misclassify expected behavior as a routing bug.\\n\\nIt especially affects:\\n- multi-agent setups,\\n- shared group chats,\\n- channels with account defaults or plugin-specific account resolution,\\n- debugging after config changes or historical binding changes.\\n\\nIt also makes it harder for both users and contributors to distinguish between:\\n- a real routing defect,\\n- expected fallback behavior,\\n- and a docs/diagnostics gap.\\n\\n#### Suggested improvement\\nI am intentionally not treating this as a confirmed bug or assuming a specific implementation.\\n\\nThe request is narrower: make inbound routing outcomes easier to explain and verify.\\n\\nThat could mean improving one or more of the following:\\n- diagnostics,\\n- observability,\\n- logs/status output,\\n- or docs that explain how to interpret routing outcomes.\\n\\nThe main goal is to make it easier to answer, for a specific inbound message:\\n- which routing path won,\\n- whether fallback was involved,\\n- and whether the observed outcome is expected.\\n\\n#### Minimal reproduction\\nObserved in local setup:\\n1. use a multi-agent environment with group traffic,\\n2. inspect visible bindings/config from the operator side,\\n3. send or observe an inbound group message that resolves to a specific agent,\\n4. inspect the final target agent/session,\\n5. notice that the final outcome is visible, but the winning routing path is not directly explained.\\n\\nThis may depend on channel/plugin configuration, account defaults, and historical bindings.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 交付 B：P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\\n\\n### 1) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md`（或对应 zh-CN 同位置）\\n**补一句：**\\n> The canonical session key shows the final routed target, but it does not by itself explain which routing rule matched.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n先把“session key 不是 routing rule 解释器”讲清。\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2) `docs/channels/channel-routing.md` 中 session key / routing precedence 相邻位置\\n**补一句：**\\n> For group chats, OpenClaw first resolves the target agent using routing precedence, then derives the canonical group session key from that result.\\n\\n**作用：**\\n明确先后顺序：先路由，后生成 canonical\n…(truncated)…"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774413579225},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" 已继续完成并回 main，但 `sessions_send` 仍超时。\n\n本次已产出两份可直接贴 GitHub 的内容：\n\n### A. P1 diagnostics gap issue v2\n包含：\n- **3 个标题备选**\n- 正文按：\n  - Background\n  - What is unclear\n  - Why this matters\n  - Suggested improvement\n- 明确写了：\n  - **this is not being presented as a confirmed bug**\n- 另附：\n  - **1 段 minimal reproduction**\n\n### B. P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\n包含：\n- **要改哪些文档位置**\n- **每处补什么一句话**\n- **为什么这是最小可合并版本**\n\n如果你要，我下一条可以把 **P1 issue 最终英文版** 单独再压成一份无解释、可直接复制提交的纯净文本。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0cc067ee97d726120169c3673d9a048191998d2084f475b4c5\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774413627576}],"truncated":true,"droppedMessages":false,"contentTruncated":true,"contentRedacted":true,"bytes":27994},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774433355154}}
{"type":"message","id":"b5f16c03","parentId":"912807fa","timestamp":"2026-03-25T10:09:15.193Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_avlQCjWDKNzxFJFBHSjMwUhF|fc_0d8886978b870ccc0169c3b44ae3048191bdb5820d2f045621","toolName":"sessions_history","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"sessionKey\": \"agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"状态：派单\\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，负责复核和找风险。\\n上下文：当前主方向是把“Feishu 群未显式绑定仍能路由”收敛为 diagnostics/docs gap，而不是先定成 bug。P1 diagnostics gap issue，P2 group session key docs PR。\\n交付要求：\\n1）审查 P1 issue framing 的风险点：哪些表述容易被 maintainer 反驳成 expected behavior。\\n2）给出 issue/PR 文案里应避免的措辞，以及建议替换说法。\\n3）补一个 maintainer 视角的 objection list + 对应应答。\\n请直接回 main，按“状态/任务/结果/原因/建议”格式。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413248363,\n      \"provenance\": {\n        \"kind\": \"inter_session\",\n        \"sourceSessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3\",\n        \"sourceChannel\": \"feishu\",\n        \"sourceTool\": \"sessions_send\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"我直接按 maintainer 视角做一轮反驳预演，整理成可直接发给 main 的复核稿。\",\n          \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_05398d4231b31a4a0169c365c451c081919999e212dcb82432\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_VXb4ljHF8ZiQaOgiBNYGNN1W|fc_05398d4231b31a4a0169c365c45bf88191a6199e48819740c8\",\n          \"name\": \"sessions_send\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"sessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n            \"message\": \"状态：成功\\n任务：复核 P1 diagnostics gap issue 与 P2 group session key docs PR 的 framing 风险，补 maintainer 视角 objection list\\n结果：\\n一、P1 issue framing 最容易被 maintainer 反驳的风险点\\n1. 把“未见显式绑定”写成“没有绑定”\\n- 风险：maintainer 会直接用 default-agent fallback、channel-only binding、account default、plugin-resolved scope、历史 binding 反驳。\\n- 更稳写法：\\n  - 避免：`there is no binding`\\n  - 改成：`no obvious explicit binding was visible from the operator's point of view`\\n  - 或：`routing happened without an obvious visible binding explanation`\\n\\n2. 把“路由到了某 agent”写成“路由错了”\\n- 风险：当前证据不足以证明 wrong routing，只能证明 explainability 不足。\\n- 更稳写法：\\n  - 避免：`messages were routed to the wrong agent`\\n  - 改成：`it was difficult to explain why the message was routed to that agent`\\n\\n3. 把 Feishu 群个案写成通用核心 bug\\n- 风险：maintainer 可能说这是 channel/plugin-specific、config-specific、historical state-specific。\\n- 更稳写法：\\n  - 避免：`OpenClaw routes group messages incorrectly`\\n  - 改成：`Observed in local Feishu group setup; may depend on channel plugin config, account defaults, or historical bindings`\\n\\n4. 把“缺少诊断面”写成“实现有缺陷”\\n- 风险：maintainer 可能认同行为本身是 expected，但不认同 bug 定性。\\n- 更稳写法：\\n  - 避免：`routing logic is broken`\\n  - 改成：`the effective routing decision is not easy to inspect`\\n\\n5. 用“random / unexpected / silently”这类带结论色彩的词\\n- 风险：这些词暗示系统失控，容易被要求先补证据。\\n- 更稳写法：\\n  - 避免：`randomly routed`, `silently fell back`\\n  - 改成：`appears to have resolved via fallback or implicit routing, but the winning rule was not visible`\\n\\n二、issue / PR 文案里应避免的措辞，以及替换说法\\n1. 避免：`bug`, `wrong routing`, `incorrect agent selection`\\n- 替换：`diagnostics gap`, `observability gap`, `hard to explain routing outcome`\\n\\n2. 避免：`without bindings`\\n- 替换：`without an obvious explicit binding visible to the operator`\\n\\n3. 避免：`OpenClaw should not do this`\\n- 替换：`It is unclear whether this is expected fallback behavior, implicit binding resolution, or a docs/diagnostics gap`\\n\\n4. 避免：`the docs are wrong`\\n- 替换：`the docs may not make this behavior easy to reason about in practice`\\n\\n5. 避免：`this proves routing is broken`\\n- 替换：`this shows the current routing decision path is hard to inspect from the operator side`\\n\\n6. 避免：`no explanation`\\n- 替换：`no direct operator-facing explanation of which routing rule won`\\n\\n7. 避免：`should be obvious`\\n- 替换：`would be easier to debug if diagnostics exposed...`\\n\\n三、maintainer 视角 objection list + 对应应答\\n1. objection：This is expected behavior. Unmatched inbound traffic falls back to the default agent.\\n- 应答：\\n  Agreed — this may be expected behavior. The issue is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule for a specific inbound message.\\n\\n2. objection：Bindings may still exist via account defaults, channel-only bindings, or historical config.\\n- 应答：\\n  Yes. That is exactly why the current operator experience is hard to reason about. The request is for better visibility into which rule actually matched, not a claim that those mechanisms are wrong.\\n\\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\\n- 应答：\\n  The observation came from a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader: operators in multi-agent setups cannot easily tell whether routing matched a binding or default fallback.\\n\\n4. objection：We already document routing precedence.\\n- 应答：\\n  The precedence is documented, but in practice it is still hard to map one observed inbound event to the specific winning rule. This request is about bridging that gap between documented rules and operator-facing diagnosis.\\n\\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\\n- 应答：\\n  A docs improvement would already help. If maintainers prefer, this can be scoped as docs/diagnostics enhancement rather than a bug report.\\n\\n6. objection：We need stronger reproduction before calling this a problem.\\n- 应答：\\n  Agreed. That is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and instead focuses on explainability and inspectability of the routing result observed in local setup.\\n\\n7. objection：Session keys already show which agent handled the message.\\n- 应答：\\n  Yes, but the canonical group session key reflects the selected agent after routing. It does not tell the operator which routing rule won, which is the missing diagnostic piece.\\n\\n四、对 P2 docs PR 的专门提醒\\n1. 不要把 docs PR 写成“修正错误文档”\\n- 更稳写法：`clarify`, `make the distinction more explicit`, `add a concrete example`\\n\\n2. 不要暗示 session key 可以反推出 routing cause\\n- 更稳写法：`session key reflects the selected target agent after routing; it does not by itself explain which routing rule won`\\n\\n3. 不要把 Feishu 个案写成 docs 普遍错误\\n- 更稳写法：`This became confusing in a local Feishu group setup, but the clarification appears useful more broadly for multi-agent group routing`\\n\\n原因：当前最怕的不是 maintainer 不认价值，而是我们自己用词过猛，把“diagnostics/docs gap”写成“routing bug”，从而在证据不足时被一句 expected behavior 打回。先把语气收稳，反而更容易拿到正面反馈。\\n建议：\\n1. P1 issue 标题和正文都坚持用 `diagnostics gap / observability gap / hard to inspect`，不要出现 `wrong agent`。\\n2. P2 docs PR 用 `clarify`、`add example`、`explain the distinction`，不要用 `fix incorrect docs`。\\n3. 如果 main 要今天就发，我建议在 issue 里主动写一句：\\n`This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.`\\n这句很能降反驳率。\",\n            \"timeoutSeconds\": 20\n          },\n          \"partialJson\": \"{\\\"sessionKey\\\":\\\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"状态：成功\\\\n任务：复核 P1 diagnostics gap issue 与 P2 group session key docs PR 的 framing 风险，补 maintainer 视角 objection list\\\\n结果：\\\\n一、P1 issue framing 最容易被 maintainer 反驳的风险点\\\\n1. 把“未见显式绑定”写成“没有绑定”\\\\n- 风险：maintainer 会直接用 default-agent fallback、channel-only binding、account default、plugin-resolved scope、历史 binding 反驳。\\\\n- 更稳写法：\\\\n  - 避免：`there is no binding`\\\\n  - 改成：`no obvious explicit binding was visible from the operator's point of view`\\\\n  - 或：`routing happened without an obvious visible binding explanation`\\\\n\\\\n2. 把“路由到了某 agent”写成“路由错了”\\\\n- 风险：当前证据不足以证明 wrong routing，只能证明 explainability 不足。\\\\n- 更稳写法：\\\\n  - 避免：`messages were routed to the wrong agent`\\\\n  - 改成：`it was difficult to explain why the message was routed to that agent`\\\\n\\\\n3. 把 Feishu 群个案写成通用核心 bug\\\\n- 风险：maintainer 可能说这是 channel/plugin-specific、config-specific、historical state-specific。\\\\n- 更稳写法：\\\\n  - 避免：`OpenClaw routes group messages incorrectly`\\\\n  - 改成：`Observed in local Feishu group setup; may depend on channel plugin config, account defaults, or historical bindings`\\\\n\\\\n4. 把“缺少诊断面”写成“实现有缺陷”\\\\n- 风险：maintainer 可能认同行为本身是 expected，但不认同 bug 定性。\\\\n- 更稳写法：\\\\n  - 避免：`routing logic is broken`\\\\n  - 改成：`the effective routing decision is not easy to inspect`\\\\n\\\\n5. 用“random / unexpected / silently”这类带结论色彩的词\\\\n- 风险：这些词暗示系统失控，容易被要求先补证据。\\\\n- 更稳写法：\\\\n  - 避免：`randomly routed`, `silently fell back`\\\\n  - 改成：`appears to have resolved via fallback or implicit routing, but the winning rule was not visible`\\\\n\\\\n二、issue / PR 文案里应避免的措辞，以及替换说法\\\\n1. 避免：`bug`, `wrong routing`, `incorrect agent selection`\\\\n- 替换：`diagnostics gap`, `observability gap`, `hard to explain routing outcome`\\\\n\\\\n2. 避免：`without bindings`\\\\n- 替换：`without an obvious explicit binding visible to the operator`\\\\n\\\\n3. 避免：`OpenClaw should not do this`\\\\n- 替换：`It is unclear whether this is expected fallback behavior, implicit binding resolution, or a docs/diagnostics gap`\\\\n\\\\n4. 避免：`the docs are wrong`\\\\n- 替换：`the docs may not make this behavior easy to reason about in practice`\\\\n\\\\n5. 避免：`this proves routing is broken`\\\\n- 替换：`this shows the current routing decision path is hard to inspect from the operator side`\\\\n\\\\n6. 避免：`no explanation`\\\\n- 替换：`no direct operator-facing explanation of which routing rule won`\\\\n\\\\n7. 避免：`should be obvious`\\\\n- 替换：`would be easier to debug if diagnostics exposed...`\\\\n\\\\n三、maintainer 视角 objection list + 对应应答\\\\n1. objection：This is expected behavior. Unmatched inbound traffic falls back to the default agent.\\\\n- 应答：\\\\n  Agreed — this may be expected behavior. The issue is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule for a specific inbound message.\\\\n\\\\n2. objection：Bindings may still exist via account defaults, channel-only bindings, or historical config.\\\\n- 应答：\\\\n  Yes. That is exactly why the current operator experience is hard to reason about. The request is for better visibility into which rule actually matched, not a claim that those mechanisms are wrong.\\\\n\\\\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\\\\n- 应答：\\\\n  The observation came from a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader: operators in multi-agent setups cannot easily tell whether routing matched a binding or default fallback.\\\\n\\\\n4. objection：We already document routing precedence.\\\\n- 应答：\\\\n  The precedence is documented, but in practice it is still hard to map one observed inbound event to the specific winning rule. This request is about bridging that gap between documented rules and operator-facing diagnosis.\\\\n\\\\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\\\\n- 应答：\\\\n  A docs improvement would already help. If maintainers prefer, this can be scoped as docs/diagnostics enhancement rather than a bug report.\\\\n\\\\n6. objection：We need stronger reproduction before calling this a problem.\\\\n- 应答：\\\\n  Agreed. That is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and inst\\n…(truncated)…\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n      \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413248366\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \" 已直接回 main。\\n\\n这轮复核重点有 3 个：\\n1. **P1 issue framing 的高风险表述**：最容易被 expected behavior 反驳的点我已经拆出来了  \\n2. **应避免措辞 + 替换说法**：包括 `wrong routing`、`no binding`、`bug` 等都给了更稳替代表达  \\n3. **maintainer objection list + 应答**：按预期 fallback、历史 binding、Feishu 特例、已有 docs 等角度都预演了一遍\\n\\n我给的核心压舱句是这句，建议 main 直接用：\\n**This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.**\",\n          \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_05398d4231b31a4a0169c365f71a1c8191ac9865040217ec8d\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"final_answer\\\"}\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n      \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413301643\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"继续执行，不用等我。\\n请做 maintainer 视角复核。\\n\\n交付：\\n1）P1 diagnostics gap issue 的 5 个风险表述（容易被打回）\\n2）每个风险表述的 safer rewrite\\n3）maintainer objection list（至少 5 条）+ 对应简短应答\\n4）结论：P1 先发 issue，还是先发 docs PR，给明确判断\\n\\n按“状态/任务/结果/原因/建议”直接回 main。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413633619,\n      \"provenance\": {\n        \"kind\": \"inter_session\",\n        \"sourceSessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3\",\n        \"sourceChannel\": \"feishu\",\n        \"sourceTool\": \"sessions_send\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \"我继续按 maintainer 视角压一轮，给 main 一版可直接决策的复核结论。\",\n          \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_05398d4231b31a4a0169c36743a0248191905f2ed44e71db29\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"commentary\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_hjS6iakMvvew1xOBT9ulNOyU|fc_05398d4231b31a4a0169c36743e7948191aafcdf7a38c6db03\",\n          \"name\": \"sessions_send\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"sessionKey\": \"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\n            \"message\": \"状态：成功\\n任务：从 maintainer 视角复核 P1 diagnostics gap issue，给出风险表述、safer rewrite、objection list，并明确先发 issue 还是 docs PR\\n结果：\\n一、P1 diagnostics gap issue 的 5 个风险表述（容易被打回）\\n1. 风险表述：`Feishu group messages were routed to the wrong agent.`\\n- safer rewrite：`In local setup, it was difficult to explain why a Feishu group message was routed to a specific agent.`\\n\\n2. 风险表述：`There was no binding, but routing still happened.`\\n- safer rewrite：`No obvious explicit binding was visible from the operator's point of view, but routing still resolved to a specific agent.`\\n\\n3. 风险表述：`This proves a routing bug in OpenClaw.`\\n- safer rewrite：`This suggests a diagnostics/observability gap: the winning routing rule was not easy to inspect.`\\n\\n4. 风险表述：`OpenClaw silently and unexpectedly falls back.`\\n- safer rewrite：`The observed outcome may have been caused by fallback or implicit binding resolution, but the operator-facing reason was not clear.`\\n\\n5. 风险表述：`The docs are wrong / inconsistent with implementation.`\\n- safer rewrite：`The current docs may not make this routing outcome easy to reason about in practice, especially in multi-agent group setups.`\\n\\n二、maintainer objection list（至少 5 条）+ 对应简短应答\\n1. objection：This is expected behavior. Unmatched inbound traffic falls back to the default agent.\\n- 应答：Agreed. The report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule.\\n\\n2. objection：You may still have channel/account/default bindings or historical bindings.\\n- 应答：Yes, and that is exactly the issue: the operator could not easily tell which rule actually matched.\\n\\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\\n- 应答：Observed in a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader for multi-agent routing.\\n\\n4. objection：Routing precedence is already documented.\\n- 应答：The precedence is documented, but the current operator experience does not clearly expose which rule won for a specific inbound message.\\n\\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\\n- 应答：A docs improvement would help, but an issue is still useful to request a diagnostics/observability surface if maintainers agree that current inspection is insufficient.\\n\\n6. objection：You need stronger reproduction before claiming a product problem.\\n- 应答：Agreed, which is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and focuses on explainability of the observed outcome.\\n\\n7. objection：The session key already shows which agent handled the message.\\n- 应答：Yes, but the canonical session key reflects the selected agent after routing; it does not explain which routing rule won.\\n\\n三、结论：P1 先发 issue，还是先发 docs PR\\n- 明确判断：**先发 P1 issue，再发 docs PR。**\\n\\n四、判断依据\\n1. P1 的核心价值在于把问题定义为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是写死在某一页文档上。\\n2. 如果先发 docs PR，maintainer 很可能只把它当“文案补充”，不会正面回应“是否需要暴露 winning routing rule”。\\n3. 先发 issue 更利于争取一个明确态度：\\n- maintainers 是否认同当前可解释性不足；\\n- 是否愿意增加日志/诊断输出；\\n- 还是仅希望通过 docs 解决。\\n4. docs PR 适合作为 P1 issue 的后续动作：当 maintainer 接受“这里确实难解释”后，再补 group routing 与 canonical session key 的澄清文档，更顺。\\n\\n原因：从 maintainer 视角，最容易打回的是“你把 expected behavior 误报成 bug”。所以要先把 issue 写成一个低冲突、可接受的 diagnostics gap 讨论入口。只要 issue 站稳，docs PR 就会更容易被接。\\n建议：\\n1. P1 issue 正文里主动放这句：\\n`This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.`\\n2. 标题坚持用：\\n`Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent`\\n3. P2 docs PR 暂时作为跟进项，不抢在 issue 前面发。\",\n            \"timeoutSeconds\": 20\n          },\n          \"partialJson\": \"{\\\"sessionKey\\\":\\\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\\\",\\\"message\\\":\\\"状态：成功\\\\n任务：从 maintainer 视角复核 P1 diagnostics gap issue，给出风险表述、safer rewrite、objection list，并明确先发 issue 还是 docs PR\\\\n结果：\\\\n一、P1 diagnostics gap issue 的 5 个风险表述（容易被打回）\\\\n1. 风险表述：`Feishu group messages were routed to the wrong agent.`\\\\n- safer rewrite：`In local setup, it was difficult to explain why a Feishu group message was routed to a specific agent.`\\\\n\\\\n2. 风险表述：`There was no binding, but routing still happened.`\\\\n- safer rewrite：`No obvious explicit binding was visible from the operator's point of view, but routing still resolved to a specific agent.`\\\\n\\\\n3. 风险表述：`This proves a routing bug in OpenClaw.`\\\\n- safer rewrite：`This suggests a diagnostics/observability gap: the winning routing rule was not easy to inspect.`\\\\n\\\\n4. 风险表述：`OpenClaw silently and unexpectedly falls back.`\\\\n- safer rewrite：`The observed outcome may have been caused by fallback or implicit binding resolution, but the operator-facing reason was not clear.`\\\\n\\\\n5. 风险表述：`The docs are wrong / inconsistent with implementation.`\\\\n- safer rewrite：`The current docs may not make this routing outcome easy to reason about in practice, especially in multi-agent group setups.`\\\\n\\\\n二、maintainer objection list（至少 5 条）+ 对应简短应答\\\\n1. objection：This is expected behavior. Unmatched inbound traffic falls back to the default agent.\\\\n- 应答：Agreed. The report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule.\\\\n\\\\n2. objection：You may still have channel/account/default bindings or historical bindings.\\\\n- 应答：Yes, and that is exactly the issue: the operator could not easily tell which rule actually matched.\\\\n\\\\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\\\\n- 应答：Observed in a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader for multi-agent routing.\\\\n\\\\n4. objection：Routing precedence is already documented.\\\\n- 应答：The precedence is documented, but the current operator experience does not clearly expose which rule won for a specific inbound message.\\\\n\\\\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\\\\n- 应答：A docs improvement would help, but an issue is still useful to request a diagnostics/observability surface if maintainers agree that current inspection is insufficient.\\\\n\\\\n6. objection：You need stronger reproduction before claiming a product problem.\\\\n- 应答：Agreed, which is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and focuses on explainability of the observed outcome.\\\\n\\\\n7. objection：The session key already shows which agent handled the message.\\\\n- 应答：Yes, but the canonical session key reflects the selected agent after routing; it does not explain which routing rule won.\\\\n\\\\n三、结论：P1 先发 issue，还是先发 docs PR\\\\n- 明确判断：**先发 P1 issue，再发 docs PR。**\\\\n\\\\n四、判断依据\\\\n1. P1 的核心价值在于把问题定义为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是写死在某一页文档上。\\\\n2. 如果先发 docs PR，maintainer 很可能只把它当“文案补充”，不会正面回应“是否需要暴露 winning routing rule”。\\\\n3. 先发 issue 更利于争取一个明确态度：\\\\n- maintainers 是否认同当前可解释性不足；\\\\n- 是否愿意增加日志/诊断输出；\\\\n- 还是仅希望通过 docs 解决。\\\\n4. docs PR 适合作为 P1 issue 的后续动作：当 maintainer 接受“这里确实难解释”后，再补 group routing 与 canonical session key 的澄清文档，更顺。\\\\n\\\\n原因：从 maintainer 视角，最容易打回的是“你把 expected behavior 误报成 bug”。所以要先把 issue 写成一个低冲突、可接受的 diagnostics gap 讨论入口。只要 issue 站稳，docs PR 就会更容易被接。\\\\n建议：\\\\n1. P1 issue 正文里主动放这句：\\\\n`This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.`\\\\n2. 标题坚持用：\\\\n`Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent`\\\\n3. P2 docs PR 暂时作为跟进项，不抢在 issue 前面发。\\\",\\\"timeoutSeconds\\\":20}\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n      \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"toolUse\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413633623\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"text\",\n          \"text\": \" 已直接回 main。\\n\\n明确判断我已经给了：\\n**P1 先发 issue，再发 docs PR。**\\n\\n核心原因：\\n- 先用 issue 把问题稳稳钉在 **diagnostics / observability gap**  \\n- 不先让 maintainer 以为我们是在把 expected behavior 误报成 bug  \\n- docs PR 作为后续动作更顺，更容易被接\\n\\n这轮也一并给了：\\n1. 5 个高风险表述  \\n2. 每个表述的 safer rewrite  \\n3. 至少 5 条 maintainer objection + 简短应答\",\n          \"textSignature\": \"{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_05398d4231b31a4a0169c3676cd72081918045bdc573d03193\\\",\\\"phase\\\":\\\"final_answer\\\"}\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"api\": \"openai-codex-responses\",\n      \"provider\": \"openai-codex\",\n      \"model\": \"gpt-5.4\",\n      \"stopReason\": \"stop\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1774413675678\n    }\n  ],\n  \"truncated\": true,\n  \"droppedMessages\": false,\n  \"contentTruncated\": true,\n  \"contentRedacted\": false,\n  \"bytes\": 24565\n}"}],"details":{"sessionKey":"agent:aoao:feishu:aoao:direct:ou_0dee72e5f9e6a83b0555fdfd161f2506","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"状态：派单\n任务：继续推进 OpenClaw 贡献项目，负责复核和找风险。\n上下文：当前主方向是把“Feishu 群未显式绑定仍能路由”收敛为 diagnostics/docs gap，而不是先定成 bug。P1 diagnostics gap issue，P2 group session key docs PR。\n交付要求：\n1）审查 P1 issue framing 的风险点：哪些表述容易被 maintainer 反驳成 expected behavior。\n2）给出 issue/PR 文案里应避免的措辞，以及建议替换说法。\n3）补一个 maintainer 视角的 objection list + 对应应答。\n请直接回 main，按“状态/任务/结果/原因/建议”格式。"}],"timestamp":1774413248363,"provenance":{"kind":"inter_session","sourceSessionKey":"agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3","sourceChannel":"feishu","sourceTool":"sessions_send"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":""},{"type":"text","text":"我直接按 maintainer 视角做一轮反驳预演，整理成可直接发给 main 的复核稿。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05398d4231b31a4a0169c365c451c081919999e212dcb82432\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_VXb4ljHF8ZiQaOgiBNYGNN1W|fc_05398d4231b31a4a0169c365c45bf88191a6199e48819740c8","name":"sessions_send","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8","message":"状态：成功\n任务：复核 P1 diagnostics gap issue 与 P2 group session key docs PR 的 framing 风险，补 maintainer 视角 objection list\n结果：\n一、P1 issue framing 最容易被 maintainer 反驳的风险点\n1. 把“未见显式绑定”写成“没有绑定”\n- 风险：maintainer 会直接用 default-agent fallback、channel-only binding、account default、plugin-resolved scope、历史 binding 反驳。\n- 更稳写法：\n  - 避免：`there is no binding`\n  - 改成：`no obvious explicit binding was visible from the operator's point of view`\n  - 或：`routing happened without an obvious visible binding explanation`\n\n2. 把“路由到了某 agent”写成“路由错了”\n- 风险：当前证据不足以证明 wrong routing，只能证明 explainability 不足。\n- 更稳写法：\n  - 避免：`messages were routed to the wrong agent`\n  - 改成：`it was difficult to explain why the message was routed to that agent`\n\n3. 把 Feishu 群个案写成通用核心 bug\n- 风险：maintainer 可能说这是 channel/plugin-specific、config-specific、historical state-specific。\n- 更稳写法：\n  - 避免：`OpenClaw routes group messages incorrectly`\n  - 改成：`Observed in local Feishu group setup; may depend on channel plugin config, account defaults, or historical bindings`\n\n4. 把“缺少诊断面”写成“实现有缺陷”\n- 风险：maintainer 可能认同行为本身是 expected，但不认同 bug 定性。\n- 更稳写法：\n  - 避免：`routing logic is broken`\n  - 改成：`the effective routing decision is not easy to inspect`\n\n5. 用“random / unexpected / silently”这类带结论色彩的词\n- 风险：这些词暗示系统失控，容易被要求先补证据。\n- 更稳写法：\n  - 避免：`randomly routed`, `silently fell back`\n  - 改成：`appears to have resolved via fallback or implicit routing, but the winning rule was not visible`\n\n二、issue / PR 文案里应避免的措辞，以及替换说法\n1. 避免：`bug`, `wrong routing`, `incorrect agent selection`\n- 替换：`diagnostics gap`, `observability gap`, `hard to explain routing outcome`\n\n2. 避免：`without bindings`\n- 替换：`without an obvious explicit binding visible to the operator`\n\n3. 避免：`OpenClaw should not do this`\n- 替换：`It is unclear whether this is expected fallback behavior, implicit binding resolution, or a docs/diagnostics gap`\n\n4. 避免：`the docs are wrong`\n- 替换：`the docs may not make this behavior easy to reason about in practice`\n\n5. 避免：`this proves routing is broken`\n- 替换：`this shows the current routing decision path is hard to inspect from the operator side`\n\n6. 避免：`no explanation`\n- 替换：`no direct operator-facing explanation of which routing rule won`\n\n7. 避免：`should be obvious`\n- 替换：`would be easier to debug if diagnostics exposed...`\n\n三、maintainer 视角 objection list + 对应应答\n1. objection：This is expected behavior. Unmatched inbound traffic falls back to the default agent.\n- 应答：\n  Agreed — this may be expected behavior. The issue is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule for a specific inbound message.\n\n2. objection：Bindings may still exist via account defaults, channel-only bindings, or historical config.\n- 应答：\n  Yes. That is exactly why the current operator experience is hard to reason about. The request is for better visibility into which rule actually matched, not a claim that those mechanisms are wrong.\n\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\n- 应答：\n  The observation came from a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader: operators in multi-agent setups cannot easily tell whether routing matched a binding or default fallback.\n\n4. objection：We already document routing precedence.\n- 应答：\n  The precedence is documented, but in practice it is still hard to map one observed inbound event to the specific winning rule. This request is about bridging that gap between documented rules and operator-facing diagnosis.\n\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\n- 应答：\n  A docs improvement would already help. If maintainers prefer, this can be scoped as docs/diagnostics enhancement rather than a bug report.\n\n6. objection：We need stronger reproduction before calling this a problem.\n- 应答：\n  Agreed. That is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and instead focuses on explainability and inspectability of the routing result observed in local setup.\n\n7. objection：Session keys already show which agent handled the message.\n- 应答：\n  Yes, but the canonical group session key reflects the selected agent after routing. It does not tell the operator which routing rule won, which is the missing diagnostic piece.\n\n四、对 P2 docs PR 的专门提醒\n1. 不要把 docs PR 写成“修正错误文档”\n- 更稳写法：`clarify`, `make the distinction more explicit`, `add a concrete example`\n\n2. 不要暗示 session key 可以反推出 routing cause\n- 更稳写法：`session key reflects the selected target agent after routing; it does not by itself explain which routing rule won`\n\n3. 不要把 Feishu 个案写成 docs 普遍错误\n- 更稳写法：`This became confusing in a local Feishu group setup, but the clarification appears useful more broadly for multi-agent group routing`\n\n原因：当前最怕的不是 maintainer 不认价值，而是我们自己用词过猛，把“diagnostics/docs gap”写成“routing bug”，从而在证据不足时被一句 expected behavior 打回。先把语气收稳，反而更容易拿到正面反馈。\n建议：\n1. P1 issue 标题和正文都坚持用 `diagnostics gap / observability gap / hard to inspect`，不要出现 `wrong agent`。\n2. P2 docs PR 用 `clarify`、`add example`、`explain the distinction`，不要用 `fix incorrect docs`。\n3. 如果 main 要今天就发，我建议在 issue 里主动写一句：\n`This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.`\n这句很能降反驳率。","timeoutSeconds":20},"partialJson":"{\"sessionKey\":\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\"message\":\"状态：成功\\n任务：复核 P1 diagnostics gap issue 与 P2 group session key docs PR 的 framing 风险，补 maintainer 视角 objection list\\n结果：\\n一、P1 issue framing 最容易被 maintainer 反驳的风险点\\n1. 把“未见显式绑定”写成“没有绑定”\\n- 风险：maintainer 会直接用 default-agent fallback、channel-only binding、account default、plugin-resolved scope、历史 binding 反驳。\\n- 更稳写法：\\n  - 避免：`there is no binding`\\n  - 改成：`no obvious explicit binding was visible from the operator's point of view`\\n  - 或：`routing happened without an obvious visible binding explanation`\\n\\n2. 把“路由到了某 agent”写成“路由错了”\\n- 风险：当前证据不足以证明 wrong routing，只能证明 explainability 不足。\\n- 更稳写法：\\n  - 避免：`messages were routed to the wrong agent`\\n  - 改成：`it was difficult to explain why the message was routed to that agent`\\n\\n3. 把 Feishu 群个案写成通用核心 bug\\n- 风险：maintainer 可能说这是 channel/plugin-specific、config-specific、historical state-specific。\\n- 更稳写法：\\n  - 避免：`OpenClaw routes group messages incorrectly`\\n  - 改成：`Observed in local Feishu group setup; may depend on channel plugin config, account defaults, or historical bindings`\\n\\n4. 把“缺少诊断面”写成“实现有缺陷”\\n- 风险：maintainer 可能认同行为本身是 expected，但不认同 bug 定性。\\n- 更稳写法：\\n  - 避免：`routing logic is broken`\\n  - 改成：`the effective routing decision is not easy to inspect`\\n\\n5. 用“random / unexpected / silently”这类带结论色彩的词\\n- 风险：这些词暗示系统失控，容易被要求先补证据。\\n- 更稳写法：\\n  - 避免：`randomly routed`, `silently fell back`\\n  - 改成：`appears to have resolved via fallback or implicit routing, but the winning rule was not visible`\\n\\n二、issue / PR 文案里应避免的措辞，以及替换说法\\n1. 避免：`bug`, `wrong routing`, `incorrect agent selection`\\n- 替换：`diagnostics gap`, `observability gap`, `hard to explain routing outcome`\\n\\n2. 避免：`without bindings`\\n- 替换：`without an obvious explicit binding visible to the operator`\\n\\n3. 避免：`OpenClaw should not do this`\\n- 替换：`It is unclear whether this is expected fallback behavior, implicit binding resolution, or a docs/diagnostics gap`\\n\\n4. 避免：`the docs are wrong`\\n- 替换：`the docs may not make this behavior easy to reason about in practice`\\n\\n5. 避免：`this proves routing is broken`\\n- 替换：`this shows the current routing decision path is hard to inspect from the operator side`\\n\\n6. 避免：`no explanation`\\n- 替换：`no direct operator-facing explanation of which routing rule won`\\n\\n7. 避免：`should be obvious`\\n- 替换：`would be easier to debug if diagnostics exposed...`\\n\\n三、maintainer 视角 objection list + 对应应答\\n1. objection：This is expected behavior. Unmatched inbound traffic falls back to the default agent.\\n- 应答：\\n  Agreed — this may be expected behavior. The issue is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule for a specific inbound message.\\n\\n2. objection：Bindings may still exist via account defaults, channel-only bindings, or historical config.\\n- 应答：\\n  Yes. That is exactly why the current operator experience is hard to reason about. The request is for better visibility into which rule actually matched, not a claim that those mechanisms are wrong.\\n\\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\\n- 应答：\\n  The observation came from a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader: operators in multi-agent setups cannot easily tell whether routing matched a binding or default fallback.\\n\\n4. objection：We already document routing precedence.\\n- 应答：\\n  The precedence is documented, but in practice it is still hard to map one observed inbound event to the specific winning rule. This request is about bridging that gap between documented rules and operator-facing diagnosis.\\n\\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\\n- 应答：\\n  A docs improvement would already help. If maintainers prefer, this can be scoped as docs/diagnostics enhancement rather than a bug report.\\n\\n6. objection：We need stronger reproduction before calling this a problem.\\n- 应答：\\n  Agreed. That is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and inst\n…(truncated)…"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774413248366},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" 已直接回 main。\n\n这轮复核重点有 3 个：\n1. **P1 issue framing 的高风险表述**：最容易被 expected behavior 反驳的点我已经拆出来了  \n2. **应避免措辞 + 替换说法**：包括 `wrong routing`、`no binding`、`bug` 等都给了更稳替代表达  \n3. **maintainer objection list + 应答**：按预期 fallback、历史 binding、Feishu 特例、已有 docs 等角度都预演了一遍\n\n我给的核心压舱句是这句，建议 main 直接用：\n**This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.**","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05398d4231b31a4a0169c365f71a1c8191ac9865040217ec8d\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774413301643},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"继续执行，不用等我。\n请做 maintainer 视角复核。\n\n交付：\n1）P1 diagnostics gap issue 的 5 个风险表述（容易被打回）\n2）每个风险表述的 safer rewrite\n3）maintainer objection list（至少 5 条）+ 对应简短应答\n4）结论：P1 先发 issue，还是先发 docs PR，给明确判断\n\n按“状态/任务/结果/原因/建议”直接回 main。"}],"timestamp":1774413633619,"provenance":{"kind":"inter_session","sourceSessionKey":"agent:main:feishu:group:oc_f68e4447ecaeb604046c3d8ef84681f3","sourceChannel":"feishu","sourceTool":"sessions_send"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":""},{"type":"text","text":"我继续按 maintainer 视角压一轮，给 main 一版可直接决策的复核结论。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05398d4231b31a4a0169c36743a0248191905f2ed44e71db29\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_hjS6iakMvvew1xOBT9ulNOyU|fc_05398d4231b31a4a0169c36743e7948191aafcdf7a38c6db03","name":"sessions_send","arguments":{"sessionKey":"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8","message":"状态：成功\n任务：从 maintainer 视角复核 P1 diagnostics gap issue，给出风险表述、safer rewrite、objection list，并明确先发 issue 还是 docs PR\n结果：\n一、P1 diagnostics gap issue 的 5 个风险表述（容易被打回）\n1. 风险表述：`Feishu group messages were routed to the wrong agent.`\n- safer rewrite：`In local setup, it was difficult to explain why a Feishu group message was routed to a specific agent.`\n\n2. 风险表述：`There was no binding, but routing still happened.`\n- safer rewrite：`No obvious explicit binding was visible from the operator's point of view, but routing still resolved to a specific agent.`\n\n3. 风险表述：`This proves a routing bug in OpenClaw.`\n- safer rewrite：`This suggests a diagnostics/observability gap: the winning routing rule was not easy to inspect.`\n\n4. 风险表述：`OpenClaw silently and unexpectedly falls back.`\n- safer rewrite：`The observed outcome may have been caused by fallback or implicit binding resolution, but the operator-facing reason was not clear.`\n\n5. 风险表述：`The docs are wrong / inconsistent with implementation.`\n- safer rewrite：`The current docs may not make this routing outcome easy to reason about in practice, especially in multi-agent group setups.`\n\n二、maintainer objection list（至少 5 条）+ 对应简短应答\n1. objection：This is expected behavior. Unmatched inbound traffic falls back to the default agent.\n- 应答：Agreed. The report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule.\n\n2. objection：You may still have channel/account/default bindings or historical bindings.\n- 应答：Yes, and that is exactly the issue: the operator could not easily tell which rule actually matched.\n\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\n- 应答：Observed in a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader for multi-agent routing.\n\n4. objection：Routing precedence is already documented.\n- 应答：The precedence is documented, but the current operator experience does not clearly expose which rule won for a specific inbound message.\n\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\n- 应答：A docs improvement would help, but an issue is still useful to request a diagnostics/observability surface if maintainers agree that current inspection is insufficient.\n\n6. objection：You need stronger reproduction before claiming a product problem.\n- 应答：Agreed, which is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and focuses on explainability of the observed outcome.\n\n7. objection：The session key already shows which agent handled the message.\n- 应答：Yes, but the canonical session key reflects the selected agent after routing; it does not explain which routing rule won.\n\n三、结论：P1 先发 issue，还是先发 docs PR\n- 明确判断：**先发 P1 issue，再发 docs PR。**\n\n四、判断依据\n1. P1 的核心价值在于把问题定义为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是写死在某一页文档上。\n2. 如果先发 docs PR，maintainer 很可能只把它当“文案补充”，不会正面回应“是否需要暴露 winning routing rule”。\n3. 先发 issue 更利于争取一个明确态度：\n- maintainers 是否认同当前可解释性不足；\n- 是否愿意增加日志/诊断输出；\n- 还是仅希望通过 docs 解决。\n4. docs PR 适合作为 P1 issue 的后续动作：当 maintainer 接受“这里确实难解释”后，再补 group routing 与 canonical session key 的澄清文档，更顺。\n\n原因：从 maintainer 视角，最容易打回的是“你把 expected behavior 误报成 bug”。所以要先把 issue 写成一个低冲突、可接受的 diagnostics gap 讨论入口。只要 issue 站稳，docs PR 就会更容易被接。\n建议：\n1. P1 issue 正文里主动放这句：\n`This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.`\n2. 标题坚持用：\n`Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent`\n3. P2 docs PR 暂时作为跟进项，不抢在 issue 前面发。","timeoutSeconds":20},"partialJson":"{\"sessionKey\":\"agent:main:feishu:default:direct:ou_5abeeb52afc248214694d8d79ab20df8\",\"message\":\"状态：成功\\n任务：从 maintainer 视角复核 P1 diagnostics gap issue，给出风险表述、safer rewrite、objection list，并明确先发 issue 还是 docs PR\\n结果：\\n一、P1 diagnostics gap issue 的 5 个风险表述（容易被打回）\\n1. 风险表述：`Feishu group messages were routed to the wrong agent.`\\n- safer rewrite：`In local setup, it was difficult to explain why a Feishu group message was routed to a specific agent.`\\n\\n2. 风险表述：`There was no binding, but routing still happened.`\\n- safer rewrite：`No obvious explicit binding was visible from the operator's point of view, but routing still resolved to a specific agent.`\\n\\n3. 风险表述：`This proves a routing bug in OpenClaw.`\\n- safer rewrite：`This suggests a diagnostics/observability gap: the winning routing rule was not easy to inspect.`\\n\\n4. 风险表述：`OpenClaw silently and unexpectedly falls back.`\\n- safer rewrite：`The observed outcome may have been caused by fallback or implicit binding resolution, but the operator-facing reason was not clear.`\\n\\n5. 风险表述：`The docs are wrong / inconsistent with implementation.`\\n- safer rewrite：`The current docs may not make this routing outcome easy to reason about in practice, especially in multi-agent group setups.`\\n\\n二、maintainer objection list（至少 5 条）+ 对应简短应答\\n1. objection：This is expected behavior. Unmatched inbound traffic falls back to the default agent.\\n- 应答：Agreed. The report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer way to confirm whether fallback was the winning rule.\\n\\n2. objection：You may still have channel/account/default bindings or historical bindings.\\n- 应答：Yes, and that is exactly the issue: the operator could not easily tell which rule actually matched.\\n\\n3. objection：This sounds Feishu-specific, not a core routing issue.\\n- 应答：Observed in a local Feishu group setup, but the underlying diagnostics problem appears broader for multi-agent routing.\\n\\n4. objection：Routing precedence is already documented.\\n- 应答：The precedence is documented, but the current operator experience does not clearly expose which rule won for a specific inbound message.\\n\\n5. objection：This belongs in docs, not an issue.\\n- 应答：A docs improvement would help, but an issue is still useful to request a diagnostics/observability surface if maintainers agree that current inspection is insufficient.\\n\\n6. objection：You need stronger reproduction before claiming a product problem.\\n- 应答：Agreed, which is why the framing avoids “wrong routing” and focuses on explainability of the observed outcome.\\n\\n7. objection：The session key already shows which agent handled the message.\\n- 应答：Yes, but the canonical session key reflects the selected agent after routing; it does not explain which routing rule won.\\n\\n三、结论：P1 先发 issue，还是先发 docs PR\\n- 明确判断：**先发 P1 issue，再发 docs PR。**\\n\\n四、判断依据\\n1. P1 的核心价值在于把问题定义为 diagnostics/observability gap，而不是写死在某一页文档上。\\n2. 如果先发 docs PR，maintainer 很可能只把它当“文案补充”，不会正面回应“是否需要暴露 winning routing rule”。\\n3. 先发 issue 更利于争取一个明确态度：\\n- maintainers 是否认同当前可解释性不足；\\n- 是否愿意增加日志/诊断输出；\\n- 还是仅希望通过 docs 解决。\\n4. docs PR 适合作为 P1 issue 的后续动作：当 maintainer 接受“这里确实难解释”后，再补 group routing 与 canonical session key 的澄清文档，更顺。\\n\\n原因：从 maintainer 视角，最容易打回的是“你把 expected behavior 误报成 bug”。所以要先把 issue 写成一个低冲突、可接受的 diagnostics gap 讨论入口。只要 issue 站稳，docs PR 就会更容易被接。\\n建议：\\n1. P1 issue 正文里主动放这句：\\n`This report is not asserting wrong routing yet; it is asking for a clearer operator-facing way to confirm which routing rule won.`\\n2. 标题坚持用：\\n`Diagnostics gap: expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent`\\n3. P2 docs PR 暂时作为跟进项，不抢在 issue 前面发。\",\"timeoutSeconds\":20}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774413633623},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" 已直接回 main。\n\n明确判断我已经给了：\n**P1 先发 issue，再发 docs PR。**\n\n核心原因：\n- 先用 issue 把问题稳稳钉在 **diagnostics / observability gap**  \n- 不先让 maintainer 以为我们是在把 expected behavior 误报成 bug  \n- docs PR 作为后续动作更顺，更容易被接\n\n这轮也一并给了：\n1. 5 个高风险表述  \n2. 每个表述的 safer rewrite  \n3. 至少 5 条 maintainer objection + 简短应答","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05398d4231b31a4a0169c3676cd72081918045bdc573d03193\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774413675678}],"truncated":true,"droppedMessages":false,"contentTruncated":true,"contentRedacted":false,"bytes":24565},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774433355186}}
{"type":"message","id":"92f24189","parentId":"b5f16c03","timestamp":"2026-03-25T10:09:15.208Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_YtnnMlZClGGib7OekEdpv53Z|fc_0d8886978b870ccc0169c3b44ae3088191a20943f6a09a5c9e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# OpenClaw Contribution Push — 2026-03-25\n\n## Current strategy\n\nDo not frame the Feishu group routing behavior as a confirmed bug.\n\nPreferred framing:\n- diagnostics gap\n- docs gap\n- observability gap\n\nCore point:\nDevelopers currently lack enough visibility to tell whether inbound routing matched an explicit binding or fell back to the default agent. Even if the runtime behavior is intentional, the missing diagnostics/docs make the behavior hard to reason about and easy to misinterpret.\n\n## P1 — Diagnostics gap issue\n\n### Candidate titles\n1. Expose whether inbound routing matched a binding or fell back to the default agent\n2. Improve routing diagnostics for inbound messages that resolve via fallback\n3. Clarify routing decisions in diagnostics when bindings are not explicitly matched\n\n### Draft issue body (v1)\n\n#### Background\nWhen testing inbound routing in Feishu group conversations, it can be difficult to determine why a message was delivered to a specific agent/session. In particular, there are cases where a group message appears to reach an agent even though there is no obvious explicit group binding visible from the operator's perspective.\n\n#### What is unclear\nAt the moment, it is hard to tell whether the routing decision came from:\n- an explicit binding match,\n- canonical session-key resolution,\n- or fallback to a default agent/path.\n\nBecause this decision is not surfaced clearly in diagnostics, operators can easily misread expected fallback behavior as a binding bug.\n\n#### Why this matters\nThis creates two problems:\n1. It slows down debugging when configuring multi-agent routing.\n2. It makes documentation harder to trust, because users cannot map the observed runtime behavior back to a clear routing explanation.\n\nEven if the current behavior is working as designed, the lack of observability makes it difficult to verify that design.\n\n#### Suggested improvement\nIt would help if OpenClaw exposed a more explicit routing explanation in diagnostics/logs/status output, for example indicating whether an inbound message:\n- matched an explicit binding,\n- resolved via a canonical session/group mapping,\n- or fell back to a default agent.\n\nThis would make routing behavior much easier to debug without presuming the current implementation is incorrect.\n\n#### Minimal reproduction (abstract)\n1. Configure Feishu with a default agent and at least one explicit binding pattern.\n2. Send a message from a group conversation that is not obviously covered by the operator's expected binding rules.\n3. Observe that the message is still routed successfully.\n4. Try to determine from current diagnostics/logs whether that happened because of an explicit binding, canonical session resolution, or fallback.\n\nCurrent difficulty: the operator can observe the result, but not the routing reason with enough confidence.\n\n## P2 — Docs PR outline\n\n### Goal\nExplain how group routing decisions relate to canonical group session keys and fallback/default-agent behavior.\n\n### Minimal doc changes\n1. Routing/bindings docs\n   - Add one paragraph explaining that successful delivery does not always imply an explicit binding match.\n   - State that canonical session resolution or default-agent fallback may also explain the outcome, depending on configuration.\n\n2. Feishu/group-chat docs\n   - Add one short example showing a group message that lands in the expected agent session even when the operator assumes a binding should have been required.\n   - Explain what to check when diagnosing that result.\n\n3. Diagnostics/troubleshooting docs\n   - Add a checklist: confirm binding, confirm session key shape, confirm fallback/default-agent settings, then compare logs.\n\n### Why this is the smallest mergeable PR\n- No behavior change required\n- Low controversy\n- Converts a confusing runtime observation into explicit operator guidance\n- Complements the diagnostics issue instead of depending on it\n\n## Current recommendation\n- First: open the diagnostics gap issue (P1)\n- Then: prepare the docs PR (P2)\n- If maintainer response suggests behavior is expected, convert that answer into precise docs wording and land P2 quickly\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774433355200}}
{"type":"message","id":"0bfac06f","parentId":"92f24189","timestamp":"2026-03-25T10:09:29.874Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0d8886978b870ccc0169c3b44c53408191995cf5cb5d9f99a7\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpw7RNRpBnd0GuBVIpxREhuhntdTFTw62kiRClbDoRY-9OyayfnTTGgw_OzojCCHVjRcwW1uNSQttj5TJbd0tWDMfna7Hq_HRzQPm_vQQX4MNosPuUKmiyafclfpUAKh6YXPjyXBV_BBJlI6fZ2CLhknF-p1E9_gBvuceUxPH-dWPWFNxI2EgwQiunEqLzhihojiL3QzcUu1VbcomDQDz1AJpRArBTiAow66IooeTu3rrMCVmrrFbt1ZdqMrZlrYNISoUbvLc7EAx5ccrCEZQ8iI7RScUrg_Ls5-sa45Ded_Ryn_quXz58edCJ7xmfLNluWjOxhfZJZNQRFUXrz7AgMzVt6Nq4k0Lmew-Bioq6uyOqRBX7gOy81zPVdmF5h_d_gM0E7Av-ARNwDcPOZ0gYdn6eifA21dHy-MfzLJRaX-uCKjWfC8Y4w73YJ138_6EVRHjDfInAmuTMC7tUMEYlfydTmmxXGmBdIwRaLo1FzXp1oWG1oqbxB_Hd687oraBJblvsprsBnx5qRZmCmPu18m0bQt0beeQa8MLzdKusUf7K49pZXybpld2hiJFYtMq0iMLbS5_tMLrkA1t9a0l-HizgkGYX2KkgXSKjyNMNc7g6mwQcj2dELYVMBRW7Cng7Gxpi5V-XOq6VGWNX5-6UFEE__mrsUfEkNkcCPMILLSymBM1SNqiXedo3OXcGirc61TFcGkN8_IFCj4fruHvn1B-8coufD5fet7AjDi6llxyrjj1r-nVKzV8elmOT8rRRhe7OvgLt_cNkYUL9d0_yn4BQoevna0Y_kZx7J4B09cbmsGIzF9sMDOOQaEwAPodsy4WORUQu6GMe8-xPvsjQ8gbKPpY3uIQw09rlKoA1xOBMgsaFzNNl88rmwOdQNsEmSRrvEZENaPtPnDEj7lzZ7b0Xt9jcvRdyYummB0KwDJVUDXo=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] 进度不差，已经往前推了一截。\n\n当前状态\n- **主方向已定**：不打“confirmed bug”，改打 **diagnostics / observability / docs gap**\n- **P1 已成型**：一版可直接发 GitHub 的英文 issue 文案已经出来了\n- **P2 也有了**：docs PR 的最小改动大纲已经整理好\n- **团队回包已到**：xixi、aoao 都交了东西，不是空转\n\n现在的实际产出\n\n### main 我这边\n我已经收敛出项目主骨架，落到文件里了：\n- `project/openclaw-contrib-2026-03-25.md`\n\n里面有：\n- 当前策略\n- P1 issue 标题备选\n- issue 正文 v1\n- minimal reproduction\n- P2 docs PR 最小改动大纲\n- 当前建议：**先 P1，再 P2**\n\n### xixi 已完成\nxixi 交了 3 块关键内容：\n\n1. **P1 证据链**\n- 现象怎么描述\n- 为什么这不是直接能下结论的 bug\n- 当前文档缺口在哪\n- 为什么用户/开发者容易误判\n\n2. **P1 英文 issue v2**\n核心句已经压稳了：\n- 重点不是“routing 错了”\n- 重点是“**Which routing rule actually won?** 现在不好判断”\n\n3. **P2 docs PR 最小大纲**\n重点是把这几个关系讲清：\n- routing decision\n- canonical session key\n- fallback/default agent\n- “看到 session key” ≠ “知道哪条规则命中”\n\n### aoao 已完成\naoao 主要做了复核和防打回：\n\n1. 列了 **5 个高风险表述**\n比如这些都不该写：\n- wrong agent\n- no binding\n- proves a bug\n- docs are wrong\n\n2. 给了 **safer rewrite**\n把措辞压成 maintainer 更容易接的版本\n\n3. 给了 **objection list**\n包括 maintainer 很可能会说的：\n- this is expected behavior\n- 可能是 account/channel/default fallback\n- 这是 Feishu 特例\n- docs 已经写过 precedence\n- 这更像 docs，不像 issue\n\n4. 给了明确结论\n- **先发 P1 issue，再发 P2 docs PR**\n\n当前判断\n- 这条线是对的\n- 现在最值钱的不是继续讨论，而是把 **P1 issue 最终版** 收敛出来，准备发\n- P2 不急着先发，避免被降格成“只是补文档”\n\n下一步我会直接干\n1. 合并我、xixi、aoao 三方内容\n2. 压成 **GitHub 可直接提交的 P1 最终英文 issue**\n3. 顺手准备 P2 的 docs 改动点，等 maintainer 反馈后立刻接 PR\n\n一句话汇报\n- **方向稳了**\n- **材料齐了**\n- **现在差最后一轮收口，就能发 P1**\n\n如果你不打断，我下一步就直接进入：\n**P1 issue 最终定稿**。","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0d8886978b870ccc0169c3b44d2b308191963b1fc6b3a49933\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":15307,"output":744,"cacheRead":24960,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41011,"cost":{"input":0.0382675,"output":0.01116,"cacheRead":0.00624,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0556675}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774433355205}}
